Second Reality - Amiga OCS/ECS port, WHDLoad install
====================================================

Files:
  SecondReality.slave   WHDLoad slave
  disk.1, disk.2        the two disk images (same as the ADFs)

Start from a shell with:
  WHDLoad SecondReality.slave

or from any WHDLoad launcher.  No icon is included; to make one, copy any
WHDLoad project icon, name it SecondReality.info and set its tooltype
Slave=SecondReality.slave.

Requirements:
  - WHDLoad 10 or newer
  - 1 MB chip memory (the demo is written for 1 MB chip, OCS/ECS)
  - about 1.8 MB of other memory (the slave keeps both disk images in
    memory, so the demo never waits for a disk or asks for disk 2)

Music quality (tooltype CUSTOM1):
  CUSTOM1=0 (default)  the 4 voice arrangement played by Paula, as on the
                       floppy version
  CUSTOM1=1            all 8 voices of the original music, mixed by the CPU
                       at 16.5 kHz: needs a fast CPU (PiStorm, 68040/060 or
                       a fast 68030), otherwise the effects slow down
  CUSTOM1=2            all 8 voices at 8.3 kHz, for slower accelerators
                       (around 25 MHz 68020/030)
  e.g.  WHDLoad SecondReality.slave CUSTOM1=1

Quit with F10 at any time (or the quit key set in WHDLoad); the demo also
returns to WHDLoad by itself after the end scroller.
